--   r-noncredit-is-a-view-inside-subjects-sam-2026-11-22: Sam's ruling that noncredit is a view inside Subjects.
--   f-noncredit-catalogs-filed-s700: the three large noncredit catalogs filed (#3662).
--   f-subject-course-panel-s700: the Subjects course panel and its per-college files (#3661).
insert into public.cpl_memory (slug,kind,title,summary,tags,status,source,verified_by,verified_at,author,event_date) values
('r-athletics-under-kine-sam-2026-11-22','decision','ATH is KINE; ATHL is no common code','Sam, 2026-11-22, in session (S700): "ATHL can be in kine. It''s for competitive athletic sports as distinguished from PE activity courses". Cerritos ATH takes the common code KINE, and ATHL is no common code. This revises his ATH to ATHL decision of 2026-11-21; the Cerritos decisions file carries the revision.',array['commons','subjects','cerritos','common-subj'],'verified','Sam in session, 2026-11-22; kb/reference/subject_code_decisions_cerritos_2026-11-21.json; cpl-project-tracker#3662','Sam',now(),'SkyGuillemot (S700)','2026-11-22'),
('r-subject-save-path-kb-curation-sam-2026-11-22','decision','Subjects saves go to kb_curation, one inserted row per decision','Sam, 2026-11-22, in session (S700), on the recommended save path: "Fine." One inserted kb_curation row per decision keyed by college, local code and band (SUBJ:cerritos|ATH|credit), the reviewer''s own sign-in, Take it back removes it; a person''s save wins over the catalog, the subject map and any recommendation; the subject map stays the statewide default by PR.',array['commons','subjects','kb_curation','write-path'],'verified','Sam in session, 2026-11-22; cpl-project-tracker#3655','Sam',now(),'SkyGuillemot (S700)','2026-11-22'),
('r-noncredit-is-a-view-inside-subjects-sam-2026-11-22','decision','Noncredit subjects are a view inside Subjects, on one list','Sam, 2026-11-22, in session (S700): "Yes, view inside subjects"; "And should be able to see all subjects on one list". No separate noncredit surface: the list opens on All subjects with a Credit and Noncredit filter that lasts the visit, and the draft noncredit title list sits at #commons/subjects/noncredit.',array['commons','subjects','noncredit'],'verified','Sam in session, 2026-11-22; cpl-project-tracker#3662','Sam',now(),'SkyGuillemot (S700)','2026-11-22'),
('f-noncredit-catalogs-filed-s700','fact','The three other large noncredit catalogs are filed','S700 (#3662), a worker filed with kb/_file_noncredit_catalogs.py: San Diego College of Continuing Education 392 courses and 44 headings, Santa Ana School of Continuing Education 263 and 29, Mt. San Antonio noncredit 477 and 8 (North Orange since S690). Santa Ana and Mt. San Antonio hold noncredit only, so their credit codes read Not read yet (96 and 136).',array['commons','subjects','noncredit','catalogs','collection'],'proposed','kb/_file_noncredit_catalogs.py; cpl-project-tracker#3662',null,null,'SkyGuillemot (S700)','2026-11-22'),
('f-subject-course-panel-s700','fact','The Subjects course panel opens a local code''s courses','S700 (#3661): a local code opens that college''s courses under it in a side panel, credit and noncredit apart, each with where it is listed (catalog, COCI or both) and its C-ID, CCN and M-ID, at #commons/subjects/<college>/<code>. kb/_build_subject_courses.py files kb/status/subject_courses/<slug>.json in the daily build, matched on college, subject code and course number.',array['commons','subjects','course-panel'],'proposed','kb/_build_subject_courses.py; tests/subject_courses_test.py; cpl-project-tracker#3661',null,null,'SkyGuillemot (S700)','2026-11-22')
on conflict (slug) do nothing;

